Z||000006||JSocha||11-20-2001||10:31 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B>Self winding watches.  They used to be the rage - your movement kept the watch wound.  With the advent of batteries and solar power, they became unnecessary technology.  Seiko has only recently reintroduced this "new" technology in it's Kinetic line.  These watches were common place in the 60's, but the technology is being advertised and ground-breaking today, simply because it's been out of circulation for so long.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>My Grandfather has one of those watches.  <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"> Of course his doesn't run anymore...then again...he doesn't move much either since he had passed away many, many years ago...so that is probably the reason why his watch isn't running anymore today. &lt;*sigh*&gt;  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
