Z||000012||loafer87gt||11-20-2001||02:45 PM||||After visting my grandparents farm i think I have decided what I am going to model. Hidden out the bush along with the collection of old tractors and cars is their old threshing machine. I thought that this has several parellels to the computer. When it was first introduced it boosted efficiency and allowed farmers to be more productive. Eventually it was phased out by more modern farming equipment, like the old computer bits I am using. I also find it interesting that the threshing machine was used by my parents and grandparents to make a living on the farm, just like how I use computers now days to earn my living doing 3d work. On a side note, I found a couple of sweet cars out in the bush including a Studebaker Presidential and a Studebaker Goldenhawk. I also found a 67 GMC truck (first year of the new body style) and a mid sixties 1 tonne truck that grandpa used to haul water. On top of that I counted no less then 10 tractors! Talk about a goldmine for old vehicles||||reg||7
